# The severing of the [[sympathetic]] [[nerve trunk]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[separation|Separation]], [[removal]] or [[deprivation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Anthony Magistrale|title=A Casebook on The Stand|publisher=w:Starmont House|year=1992|page=135|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/A_Casebook_on_The_Stand/jO8sVGuNRXMC?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22moral+lobotomy%22&pg=PA135&printsec=frontcover|text=Yet this conscience is a deep part of the soul; to silence it, characters must perform a kind of moral '''lobotomy''', excising the best parts of themselves, until what is left becomes less than human.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Megan Crawford; Richard Edwards; Lesley Kidd|title=Taking Issue: Debates in Guidance and Counselling in Learning|publisher=w:Routledge|year=1998|page=51|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/_/yBfp3shYJ40C?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22cultural+lobotomy%22&pg=PA51|text=Organisations which set out to treat all individuals as the same, or are ‘colour-blind’ in their philosophy, could be said to impose a form of cultural '''lobotomy''' on their clients, in denying the additional skills, knowledge and experience that they have as members of a minority culture.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ron Elsdon|title=Affiliation in the Workplace: Value Creation in the New Organization|publisher=w:ABC-Clio|year=2002|month=October|page=21|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Affiliation_in_the_Workplace/spHDEAAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22ethical+lobotomy%22&pg=PA21&printsec=frontcover|text=Put another way, how can we avoid an ethical '''lobotomy''' in establishing an organizational perspective?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=David Resnick|title=Representing Education in Film: How Hollywood Portrays Educational Thought, Settings, and Issues|publisher=w:Palgrave Macmillan US|year=2018|month=January|page=13|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Representing_Education_in_Film/p-5FDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22social+lobotomy%22&pg=PA138&printsec=frontcover|text=In the end, as Levinson feared, the price of Charlie being accepted into normative school society is a kind of social '''lobotomy''': he is tamed, so he is not really Charlie anymore.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Leo Zaibert|title=Rethinking Punishment|publisher=w:Cambridge University Press|year=2018|month=March|page=74|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Rethinking_Punishment/SLpQDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22moral+lobotomy%22&pg=PA74&printsec=frontcover|text=From Tadros’s perspective — the perspective of classical utilitarianism — there is nothing objectionable about this moral '''lobotomy''' whereby a wrongdoer pops a moral anesthetic pill immediately after committing whatever atrocity one could imagine in order to avoid suffering — provided, that is, that she would “understand” the wrongness of her actions.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jeanne Daly|title=Ethical Intersections: Health Research, Methods And Researcher Responsibility|publisher=w:Taylor & Francis|year=2019|month=March|origyear=1996|page=200|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Ethical_Intersections/i3ekDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22intellectual+lobotomy%22&pg=PT200&printsec=frontcover|text=We might be able to offer some sort of mental rehabilitation for clinicians who suffer from this type of intellectual '''lobotomy'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Paul Wassmann|title=The Hidden Pathways of Germanic Mythology: On the Neglected, Demonized, Repulsed and Repressed Archetypical Representations of Original Germanic Culture|publisher=Chiron Publications|year=2019|month=June|page=295|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/The_Hidden_Pathways_of_Germanic_Mytholog/cjqlDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22cultural+lobotomy%22&pg=PT295&printsec=frontcover|text=For the surviving generations, in particular the post-World War II generation and their children, a time of cultural '''lobotomy''' began, accompanied by a fundamental sense of shame for the abuse carried out in the name of the nation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Lou Turner; Helen Neville|title=Frantz Fanon’s Psychotherapeutic Approaches to Clinical Work: Practicing Internationally with Marginalized Communities|publisher=w:Taylor & Francis|year=2019|month=December|page=67|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Frantz_Fanon_s_Psychotherapeutic_Approac/RGPBDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22ethical+lobotomy%22&pg=PT67&printsec=frontcover|text=The offender’s acceptance of his condemnation presupposes the coherent ensemble of collective consciousness of a specific ethical universe; that is, for an offender to recognize his act as criminal before a judge is to disapprove of the act and to negate his rupture of the public sphere by his private conduct. The North African refuses this ethical '''lobotomy''' by denial and retraction of his confession.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Dana Villa|title=Socratic Citizenship|publisher=w:Princeton University Press|year=2020|month=September|page=302|pageurl=https://www.google.com.sv/books/edition/Socratic_Citizenship/Wc3xDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22intellectual+lobotomy%22&pg=PA302&printsec=frontcover|text=It is as if civic engagement required a moral-intellectual '''lobotomy''', the better to overcome doubts about the inherent goodness of the community, the moral worth of a given group identity, or the value of specific ideological commitment.}}

